    "description": "🗃️ Grouped attribute-view (database) operations. Use the "action" field to select the operation.

Common actions: get, render_attribute_view, get_attribute_view_keys, get_attribute_view_filter_sort, search, get_primary_key_values. Required fields: get: id; render_attribute_view: no additional fields; get_attribute_view_keys: id; get_attribute_view_filter_sort: id; search: keyword; get_primary_key_values: avID.

Additional actions: add_rows, remove_rows, add_column, remove_column, set_cell, batch_set_cells, duplicate_block. Read siyuan://help/action/av/{action} for details, or call action="help" if resources are unavailable.

Parameter contract per action (fields outside the action's optional list should not be sent):
av.get: required [id] | optional []
av.render_attribute_view: required [] | optional [id, blockID, viewID, page, pageSize, query, groupPaging, createIfNotExist]
av.get_attribute_view_keys: required [id] | optional []
av.get_attribute_view_filter_sort: required [id] | optional [blockID]
av.search: required [keyword] | optional [excludes]
av.add_rows: required [avID, blockIDs] | optional [blockID, viewID, groupID, previousID, ignoreDefaultFill]
av.remove_rows: required [avID, srcIDs] | optional [blockID]
av.add_column: required [avID, keyName, keyType] | optional [blockID, keyID, keyIcon, previousKeyID]
av.remove_column: required [avID] | optional [blockID, keyID, columnID, removeRelationDest]
av.set_cell: required [avID, rowID, columnID, valueType] | optional [blockID, text, number, numberFormat, date, endDate, includeTime, checked, option, options, relationBlockIDs, url, email, phone, assets]
av.batch_set_cells: required [avID, items] | optional [blockID]
av.duplicate_block: required [avID] | optional [previousID]
av.get_primary_key_values: required [avID] | optional [keyword, page, pageSize]

AV actions operate on real SiYuan attribute views (database blocks), not Markdown tables. To initialize a new AV definition, call av(action="render_attribute_view", blockID, createIfNotExist=true). MCP can generate the AV ID automatically, materialize the NodeAttributeView block in the target document, and verify the database block registration before follow-up writes.",
    "overview": {
      "actionSummaries": {
        "add_column": "Use avID + keyName + keyType, and optionally keyID or blockID. MCP generates keyID automatically when omitted. Supported keyType values match the 16 SiYuan addable column types, including keyType="mSelect", keyType="mAsset", and keyType="lineNumber". Optional blockID must be a registered database block for this AV if you need to pin a specific block view.",
        "add_rows": "Use avID + blockIDs to add existing blocks as rows. Optional blockID/viewID/groupID/previousID refine the insertion target and preserve the intended database-block view/group defaults. MCP now polls briefly after insertion and only reports success when each source blockID resolves to exactly one writable rowID. To add a row with initial cell values, follow add_rows with av(action="batch_set_cells", avID, items=[{rowID, columnID, valueType, ...}, ...]); reuse the rowID returned by add_rows (each blockID maps to exactly one rowID).",
        "batch_set_cells": "Use avID + items[]. Each item requires rowID + columnID + valueType and its matching typed field. Optional blockID must be a registered database block for this AV if you need to pin a specific block view. MCP rejects cell value IDs and source block IDs, and suggests the matching row item ID when it can. valueType="mAsset" accepts assets[].",
        "duplicate_block": "MCP first calls the kernel duplicate API, then inserts the duplicated NodeAttributeView block into the document tree. By default it inserts after the source database block; provide previousID to override the insertion target.",
        "get": "Use an attribute view ID. Returns the full AV payload after permission checks.",
        "get_attribute_view_filter_sort": "Use id + blockID to return the filters and sorts applied to that database block view.",
        "get_attribute_view_keys": "Use id to return database keys/columns for a block-bound attribute view.",
        "get_primary_key_values": "Returns the AV name plus primary-key rows, with optional keyword/page/pageSize filtering.",
        "remove_column": "Use avID + keyID, and optionally blockID to target a specific registered database block. removeRelationDest only matters for relation columns.",
        "remove_rows": "Use avID + srcIDs to remove rows from the AV. Optional blockID pins a specific registered database block when you need explicit block-view context.",
        "render_attribute_view": "Use id plus optional blockID/viewID/page/pageSize/query to render database rows with the active view context. With createIfNotExist=true, blockID becomes the creation target; if id is omitted, MCP generates one and materializes the database block automatically. The returned materialized blockID identifies the registered database block if you need to pin a specific block view later.",
        "search": "Searches AV/database definitions by keyword and post-filters unreadable results. Unresolvable matches remain discoverable in unresolvedResults, alongside raw result counts and filtering reasons. Match scope primarily covers AV names plus primary-key fallback results, not arbitrary cell text.",
        "set_cell": "Use avID + rowID + columnID + valueType and the matching typed field. rowID must be the AV row item ID stored in value.blockID, not value.id or the bound source block ID. Optional blockID must be a registered database block for this AV if you need to pin a specific block view. valueType="mAsset" accepts assets[] plus optional text markdown.",
      },
      "actions": {
        "add_column": {
          "hint": "Use avID + keyName + keyType, and optionally keyID or blockID. MCP generates keyID automatically when omitted. Supported keyType values match the 16 SiYuan addable column types, including keyType="mSelect", keyType="mAsset", and keyType="lineNumber". Optional blockID must be a registered database block for this AV if you need to pin a specific block view.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "add_rows": {
          "hint": "Use avID + blockIDs to add existing blocks as rows. Optional blockID/viewID/groupID/previousID refine the insertion target and preserve the intended database-block view/group defaults. MCP now polls briefly after insertion and only reports success when each source blockID resolves to exactly one writable rowID. To add a row with initial cell values, follow add_rows with av(action="batch_set_cells", avID, items=[{rowID, columnID, valueType, ...}, ...]); reuse the rowID returned by add_rows (each blockID maps to exactly one rowID).",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "batch_set_cells": {
          "hint": "Use avID + items[]. Each item requires rowID + columnID + valueType and its matching typed field. Optional blockID must be a registered database block for this AV if you need to pin a specific block view. MCP rejects cell value IDs and source block IDs, and suggests the matching row item ID when it can. valueType="mAsset" accepts assets[].",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "duplicate_block": {
          "hint": "MCP first calls the kernel duplicate API, then inserts the duplicated NodeAttributeView block into the document tree. By default it inserts after the source database block; provide previousID to override the insertion target.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "get": {
          "hint": "Use an attribute view ID. Returns the full AV payload after permission checks.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "get_attribute_view_filter_sort": {
          "hint": "Use id + blockID to return the filters and sorts applied to that database block view.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "get_attribute_view_keys": {
          "hint": "Use id to return database keys/columns for a block-bound attribute view.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "get_primary_key_values": {
          "hint": "Returns the AV name plus primary-key rows, with optional keyword/page/pageSize filtering.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "remove_column": {
          "hint": "Use avID + keyID, and optionally blockID to target a specific registered database block. removeRelationDest only matters for relation columns.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "remove_rows": {
          "hint": "Use avID + srcIDs to remove rows from the AV. Optional blockID pins a specific registered database block when you need explicit block-view context.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "render_attribute_view": {
          "hint": "Use id plus optional blockID/viewID/page/pageSize/query to render database rows with the active view context. With createIfNotExist=true, blockID becomes the creation target; if id is omitted, MCP generates one and materializes the database block automatically. The returned materialized blockID identifies the registered database block if you need to pin a specific block view later.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "search": {
          "hint": "Searches AV/database definitions by keyword and post-filters unreadable results. Unresolvable matches remain discoverable in unresolvedResults, alongside raw result counts and filtering reasons. Match scope primarily covers AV names plus primary-key fallback results, not arbitrary cell text.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
        "set_cell": {
          "hint": "Use avID + rowID + columnID + valueType and the matching typed field. rowID must be the AV row item ID stored in value.blockID, not value.id or the bound source block ID. Optional blockID must be a registered database block for this AV if you need to pin a specific block view. valueType="mAsset" accepts assets[] plus optional text markdown.",
          "requiresConfirmation": false,
        },
      },
      "advancedActions": [
        "add_rows",
        "remove_rows",
        "add_column",
        "remove_column",
        "set_cell",
        "batch_set_cells",
        "duplicate_block",
      ],
      "commonActions": [
        "get",
        "render_attribute_view",
        "get_attribute_view_keys",
        "get_attribute_view_filter_sort",
        "search",
        "get_primary_key_values",
      ],
      "detailsHint": "Call av(action="help", topic="<actionName>") for required fields, shapes, and a minimal example.",
      "guidance": [
        "AV actions operate on real SiYuan attribute views (database blocks), not Markdown tables.",
        "To initialize a new AV definition, call av(action="render_attribute_view", blockID, createIfNotExist=true). MCP can generate the AV ID automatically, materialize the NodeAttributeView block in the target document, and verify the database block registration before follow-up writes.",
        "Use strong typed fields such as valueType=text/number/date/checkbox/select when calling av(action="set_cell") or av(action="batch_set_cells").",
        "For cell writes, rowID must be the database row item ID stored in each AV value's blockID field. The value id field is only the cell value ID, and block.id is the original bound source block ID.",
        "AV permission checks resolve from registered database blocks. For createIfNotExist=true, provide blockID as the creation target; once materialized, MCP reuses the registered database block automatically.",
        "av(action="search") first queries kernel search results, then MCP post-filters unreadable or unresolvable AVs and reports the filtering metadata.",
        "av(action="search") is best for database names and primary-key matches. Do not assume it will find arbitrary non-primary-key cell text immediately after writes.",
      ],
      "helpResources": [
        "siyuan://help/action/av/{action}",
        "siyuan://help/tool-overview",
        "siyuan://help/examples",
        "siyuan://help/ai-layout-guide",
      ],
      "tool": "av",
    },
  },
  "block": {
    "actions": {
      "append": {
        "action": "append",
        "example": {
          "action": "append",
          "data": "- New item",
          "dataType": "markdown",
          "parentID": "20240318112233-abc123",
        },
        "fullDocResource": "siyuan://help/action/block/append",
        "guidance": [
          "block(action="prepend") or block(action="append") with a document ID targets the document start or end.",
          "block(action="update") is best for single-block replacement. Multi-line markdown may be truncated to the first line by SiYuan; use append/prepend/insert when you need multiple blocks, tables, or longer multi-line content.",
          "block(action="prepend") or block(action="append") with a block ID targets that block's child list.",
          "To create real SiYuan tags inside markdown content, use the syntax #tag# with both leading and trailing # characters.",
          "To turn a block into a flashcard, prefer flashcard(action="create_card"). It writes "custom-riff-decks" and registers the riff card together.",
          "block(action="set_fold_state") requires a foldable block ID, not a document ID.",
          "block(action="recent_updated") is read-only; MCP filters unreadable notebooks first and then applies count.",
          "block(action="recent_updated") now presents the document-grouped summary as the primary user-facing view while keeping the raw block stream for advanced consumers.",
        ],
        "hint": "parentID can be either a document ID or block ID; behavior differs. Returns a slim success object with the created block ID. Prefer append when you need to add multi-line markdown, tables, or multiple new blocks. Use #tag# syntax in markdown when you want SiYuan to register a real tag.",
        "requiredFields": [
          "dataType",
          "data",
          "parentID",
        ],
        "requiresConfirmation": false,
        "shapes": [
