    "description": "🔍 Grouped search and query operations. Use the "action" field to select the operation.

Common actions: fulltext, query_sql, search_tag, get_backlinks, get_backmentions. Required fields: fulltext: query; query_sql: stmt; search_tag: k; get_backlinks: id; get_backmentions: id.

Additional actions: search_refs, find_replace, search_assets, get_asset_content, fulltext_asset_content, list_invalid_refs. Read siyuan://help/action/search/{action} for details, or call action="help" if resources are unavailable.

Parameter contract per action (fields outside the action's optional list should not be sent):
search.fulltext: required [query] | optional [method, methodName, types, typeShortcodes, paths, groupBy, orderBy, sortBy, page, pageSize, parentId, hasTags, stripHtml]
search.query_sql: required [stmt] | optional [sql]
search.search_tag: required [k] | optional [query]
search.get_backlinks: required [id] | optional [keyword, refTreeID, scopeRootId]
search.get_backmentions: required [id] | optional [keyword, refTreeID, scopeRootId]
search.search_refs: required [id] | optional [rootID, k, beforeLen, isSquareBrackets, isDatabase, reqId]
search.find_replace: required [k, r, ids] | optional [paths, types, method, methodName, orderBy, sortBy, groupBy, replaceTypes]
search.search_assets: required [k] | optional [query, exts]
search.get_asset_content: required [id, query] | optional [queryMethod]
search.fulltext_asset_content: required [query] | optional [types, method, methodName, orderBy, sortBy, page, pageSize]
search.list_invalid_refs: required [] | optional [page, pageSize]

All search actions are read-only except find_replace, which modifies content and requires explicit user confirmation. search(action="query_sql") only accepts SELECT statements; mutation queries will be rejected, and returned rows are filtered by notebook permission. When calling query_sql, always add LIMIT yourself. MCP may still truncate large result sets and will tell you when to refine the query. The blocks table columns include: id, parent_id, root_id, box, path, hpath, name, alias, memo, tag, content, fcontent, markdown, length, type, subtype, ial, sort, created, updated. In SQL results, blocks.type uses SiYuan short codes such as d=document, h=heading, p=paragraph, l=list, i=list-item, b=blockquote, c=code, m=math, t=table, html=html, video=video, audio=audio, widget=widget. Requires user confirmation before: find_replace.",
    "overview": {
      "actionSummaries": {
        "find_replace": "This is the mutating exception inside the search tool. It performs content replacement after write-permission checks and still requires explicit user confirmation.",
        "fulltext": "Pass a query string. Supports keyword, query syntax, SQL, and regex modes via methodName (preferred) or method. fulltext now returns plainContent/excerpt by default. types accepts shortcodes directly: {"h": true, "c": true} auto-expands to {"heading": true, "codeBlock": true}. Use sortBy="relevance" or "date" instead of numeric orderBy. Use parentId to scope within a document, hasTags to filter tagged blocks.",
        "fulltext_asset_content": "Searches indexed asset/OCR text. Prefer methodName and sortBy over numeric method/orderBy. Typical flow: use this to discover matching asset-content ids, then call get_asset_content for a specific record.",
        "get_asset_content": "Reads one asset-content record by id + query. Typical flow: first discover candidate asset-content ids with fulltext_asset_content, then call get_asset_content for the exact match you want to inspect.",
        "get_backlinks": "Returns documents/blocks that contain a reference ((ref)) to the given block ID. Partial permission-filtered results include machine-readable metadata.",
        "get_backmentions": "Returns documents/blocks that mention the name of the given block (text mention, not ref link). Partial permission-filtered results include machine-readable metadata.",
        "list_invalid_refs": "no extra fields",
        "query_sql": "Execute a SELECT statement. Common tables: blocks, spans, assets. Prefer sql over stmt when prompting an AI. Always use LIMIT to control result size. MCP returns data plus truncation and permission-filtering metadata when applicable.",
